  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_a6e2f6dc51a74a52a2a9c237a0424c26",
      "statement": "Runnable is the foundational execution abstraction in LangChain's core layer, defining a generic interface (Runnable[Input, Output]) that requires only the abstract invoke() method implementation; all other execution methods (ainvoke, batch, abatch, stream, astream) have default implementations that subclasses can override for optimization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L197-L329",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0fc61d0018b1cfc55713f48b37f8f3976dad338a6308acca0e81f0b18db43343:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L949-L970",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1eff67928434ddfbed49df8733ced09fcdcaed9685752f6d6c2a1cc572f78aae:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1d4c47c26ed54403bc20048bd3a40c43",
      "statement": "All Runnables must implement invoke(input, config=None) to transform a single input into an output synchronously, while ainvoke() delegates to sync via run_in_executor by default. Similarly, stream() yields a single output from invoke() by default, while specialized implementations (chat models, streaming parsers) override to yield partial outputs incrementally.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L1258-L1277",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23cc3478740b415df53cc79cbb93700be85319defdec671ee846f03b1fd9f5ea:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L949-L970",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1eff67928434ddfbed49df8733ced09fcdcaed9685752f6d6c2a1cc572f78aae:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L972-L993",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b913e2c72cc2dc393ea9a9a5d0e771107d317467deae11c5429aef7f2919f50f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e97522466a345999f0845b1ee976c5c",
      "statement": "The batch(inputs, config, return_exceptions) method processes multiple inputs in parallel using ThreadPoolExecutor by default, and accepts either a single config applied to all inputs or a list of configs (one per input). Subclasses override for batching-aware backends like LLM batch APIs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L995-L1043",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:162e8b332e60ac819bd13d160c07a848461973a135ccbc10cf7ca5337413b062:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2dd735b9b7a5432da1b4c220d631325f",
      "statement": "The abatch() method calls ainvoke() for each input concurrently via asyncio.gather and respects max_concurrency from config to limit parallelism via gather_with_concurrency.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L1130-L1176",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b73d0df1686a61b4e167421bba0bc63c64ef368e8d846611a58721b9b6bb2dc4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_132c9ec3445842cb9e6f057114f57cca",
      "statement": "Runnables expose input_schema and output_schema properties as Pydantic models inferred from generic type parameters or implementer-provided type hints. config_schema(include=None) returns a Pydantic model for fields marked as configurable via configurable_fields() or configurable_alternatives(), enabling runtime behavior configuration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L374-L527",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d4bd62ab54422fba251b17506891ac57c18684938cd1d0d71a27cda790770a3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_80c6032920904a8bbc8de625f95945f7",
      "statement": "The __or__() operator creates a RunnableSequence by composing runnables sequentially; `other` can be a Runnable, callable, dict (coerced to RunnableParallel), or RunnableLike. The operator automatically flattens nested RunnableSequences for efficiency.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L648-L722",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:60c8a9355f19918ea595f3722b42293719d828ee6b3dc539d94abb2bdf863b90:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_78824918d29a4856b9884c70aae3cf0d",
      "statement": "RunnableSequence chains multiple Runnables sequentially where each output feeds into the next input. It optimizes batch and stream operations by calling each step's batch/stream method in order. If all steps implement transform(), the sequence chains them for end-to-end streaming; otherwise, streaming begins after the last blocking step.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L3094-L3250",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e17c9b4d22b465eb4fe938622668409ee9d6c526c045b1b81b976345954edad:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_100ba4a52e44449282a69c29150b9bcd",
      "statement": "RunnableParallel invokes multiple Runnables concurrently with the same input and collects results into a dict. It can be instantiated directly or via a dict literal in a sequence. Sync invoke uses thread pool executor; async ainvoke uses asyncio.gather with concurrency control from max_concurrency.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L3883-L3965",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51a7d6b77803d9585e4f749ba8bcd2a3b2e403611c448b758555156df662e148:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d460f4a5dc7e40bcad6300f3e275265b",
      "statement": "RunnableBranch selects and runs one of several branches based on condition evaluation. It accepts (condition, runnable) tuples plus a final default runnable. Conditions are themselves Runnables that return bool; they are evaluated sequentially, and the first True condition selects its runnable. It supports both sync and async conditions natively.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/branch.py#L43-L290",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77b53fbabf2bdae2e052b15b90650cf13e0e2d73221231eb5f782f4a5b5445ed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_69404fc2cef3419f9986f5580da9a18e",
      "statement": "RunnableConfig is a TypedDict carrying execution context (tags, metadata, callbacks, run_name, max_concurrency, recursion_limit, configurable, run_id) through chains. Config is threaded via context variables and explicit parameter passing; merge_configs() combines parent and child configs with child values taking precedence and lists being concatenated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/config.py#L57-L129",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:def5c5af24438aa68655c3dd7c5616745bc16d1e92d9f85b281622790264a60d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4d3d983232674c78983aadc573e45a6c",
      "statement": "RunnableLambda wraps a Python callable into a Runnable. If a lambda returns a Runnable, that runnable is automatically invoked. It does not support streaming by default (use RunnableGenerator for streaming). It automatically detects async callables and provides native async support, and infers input/output types from function signatures.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L4722-L4768",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c093cf9789c1bb0196cb8fbea7c605109e15836779a5463d9c53cd963c74a5fb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_69516317616242d48733a2eb8ce08288",
      "statement": "RunnableGenerator wraps generator functions (sync or async) to create streaming runnables. It implements transform() and atransform() to enable end-to-end streaming through chains where partial outputs flow as they are generated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L4418-L4465",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d635e57fe13cfe62bfff315d561c0cb74b605d9b3e1d85a7e84a7867242d3c7d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5c129dd294a84fafa705ee9da6461ccb",
      "statement": "RunnableWithFallbacks invokes a primary runnable, then each fallback in order until one succeeds. It catches exceptions matching exceptions_to_handle and proceeds to the next fallback. If exception_key is set, handled exceptions are injected into the input dict before invoking the next fallback. Both ainvoke() and abatch() are natively async; batch handling tracks per-input success/failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/fallbacks.py#L37-L590",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a9f0c0e55d40ef5e37229535b9d3b42ed1860dee6a6511d13934e69d3f272c2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9a186698a4044dff9e8d764c39874ac7",
      "statement": "The with_retry() method wraps a Runnable to add retry logic powered by tenacity. It accepts retry_if_exception_type (tuple or callable), stop_after_attempt (default 3), and wait_exponential_jitter (default True). For batches, it retries only failed inputs. Stream and transform are not retried due to ambiguous semantics.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L2153-L2200",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fafbce36a0743113eb474c823aefc8edd6f7cdf5c6318b7bcd0a55cf320dee7b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bfee11b702c946c0886b361e63206670",
      "statement": "RunnablePassthrough passes input through unchanged. It is useful in parallel branches to preserve the original input for later composition steps.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/passthrough.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:260de5bbbc388123f43ef30b9c4625e3e4748fd4c378db5f2f646347dc8bf556"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e713c8229f724a5a9167daf93f279e92",
      "statement": "coerce_to_runnable() converts any RunnableLike into a Runnable: already-Runnable objects pass through, generators are wrapped in RunnableGenerator, callables are wrapped in RunnableLambda, and dicts are coerced to RunnableParallel. This enables intuitive composition syntax like prompt | my_function | {\"field\": another_function}.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L6595-L6668",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:38722d50a08e38015e97c35aa89ed7323042001a3336814767b6e9170f84af30:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e28b4a721464876a602f7c5ffb2a225",
      "statement": "Streaming is a first-class execution mode in Runnables. The default stream() yields a single output from invoke(), but specialized implementations override to yield partial outputs. The transform(input_iterator) method maps streams of inputs to streams of outputs without blocking, enabling progressive end-to-end streaming through entire chains.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L1258-L1277",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23cc3478740b415df53cc79cbb93700be85319defdec671ee846f03b1fd9f5ea:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L1824-L1861",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:38fa23841ba51534b75041fe2cd9eec541ee2c5017c1c91d51108441a504b9ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_acbe40c18b984ab696b8a024aca90ffd",
      "statement": "Composition methods (with_fallbacks, with_retry, pick, assign, pipe) return new Runnable instances without mutating the original. This enables safe chaining and component reuse without side effects.",
      "evidence": [
